**1. `degreeDecrease` changes the end multiplicities in the wrong direction.**

```cpp
void gsCompactKnotVector<T>::degreeDecrease(int const & i)
{
    m_p -= i;
    increaseMultFirst(i);   // should decrease
    increaseMultLast (i);
}
```

This looks copied from `degreeIncrease` with only the `m_p` update flipped. For a clamped (open) knot vector, the end knots have multiplicity `p+1`. Lowering the degree by `i` must therefore remove `i` copies from each end.

This code instead adds `i` copies to each end. The end multiplicities become `p_old + 1 + i`, while the new degree is `p_old - i`, so each end exceeds the required `p_new + 1` by `2i`. That breaks the invariant that `size() - m_p - 1` equals the number of basis functions. It also corrupts anything derived from it, such as `greville_into`, which sizes its result from `this->size() - m_p - 1`.

The fix is to decrease the end multiplicities, either through a `decreaseMultFirst/Last` pair or with the same arithmetic `trim(i)` performs.

**2. `trim` is defined on the wrong class.**

```cpp
template <class T>
void gsKnotVector<T>::trim(int i)
{
    std::transform(m_mult_sum.begin(), ...);
    m_mult_sum.back() -= i;
}
```

